Z||000014||TI_3VOM||06-22-2001||03:56 PM||||I wouldn't say I talk to my Fiero, but I always congratulate it after getting me out of a jam. Best Example: I'm at a red light when a Ford "Mudstain" pulls up next to me, gunning his motor. The light turns green, and, due to the light drizzle earlier that evening, he winds up fishtailing all over the place, trying to accelerate out of it. I'm just edging him out in my lane, waving to him as I pass him and get ahead. He eventually got his traction back, but not before having to slide in behind me (parked cars ahead of him in his lane).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Another thing I do is kiss my hand and "pass it on" to my car by touching the roof. I do this when passing through a yellow light. <BR>I supposed to bring good luck against any over-zealous traffic cops.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||4
